// ============================================================================
// ⚠⚠ RETIRED BY (owner decision OD-3, 2026-09-01) ⚠⚠
//
// This model is NO LONGER THE SOURCE OF TRUTH. Every row was migrated into
// `AiRoutingPolicy` as an `isDefault = true` provider configuration, and
// `AiRoutingPolicy` is now where "which provider + model serves task X for
// tenant Y" is decided. See `ai-routing-policy.prisma`.
//
// **OD-3 explicitly reverses ruling that `AiTaskDefault` survives.**
// The reversal instrument is; the reason is finding F-7 — this model's
// `@@unique([tenantId, taskKey])` permits EXACTLY ONE row per task, so there is
// nowhere to put a second candidate and no default election to hold. The
// product requires many configurations per task with one elected default, which
// this shape cannot express at any amount of application code.
//
// ## Why the table still exists (a staged retirement, not an oversight)
//
// The table survives one release as a READ-COMPATIBILITY PROJECTION, because
// dropping it in the same change would stop day-1 inference:
//
//   * `apps/guardrail` reads `core."AiTaskDefault"` ⋈ `core."AiModel"` over its
//     own read-only SQL connection (`core/tenant_config.py`, the sanctioned
//     peer-service exception) — a CROSS-LANGUAGE reader that no TypeScript
//     change can repoint; and
//   * ~40 TypeScript call sites resolve through `AiTaskDefaultService`.
//
// So `AiTaskDefaultService.upsertRow` now WRITES THROUGH: it writes the
// authoritative `AiRoutingPolicy` row and the projection row inside ONE
// transaction, so the two cannot drift, and a test asserts they agree. This is
// a strangler-fig transition with a stated end condition, not a second home for
// the data.
//
// ## What must happen before this table is dropped — TASK-862 status
//
// /// @deprecated TASK-862 — removed in R3.
//
//   1. DONE (TASK-862): `apps/guardrail/.../core/tenant_config.py` reads
//      `AiRoutingPolicy` ⋈ `AiModel` (by `modelId`); NOTHING reads this table.
//   2. DONE (TASK-862): `AiTaskDefaultService` is a FACADE over
//      `AiRoutingPolicyService.resolveDefault`; it never reads or writes this
//      table. The ~40 TypeScript readers still call the facade (same interface)
//      and are repointed one by one to `IAiRoutingPolicyService.resolveDefault`
//      — the follow-up the orchestrator schedules after the TASK-859 wave merges.
//   3. R3: delete the service, its controller, the console screen and
//      `packages/vox-node/src/resources/admin/ai-task-default.ts`;
//   4. R3: drop the table (its rows are already inert — no writer exists).
//
// Do NOT add a new reader, a new writer, or a new row to this model.
// ============================================================================
// AI Task Defaults
//
// Per-tenant "default model for task X" selector — the Class-3 generalization
// of HarnessPolicy.textProvider/textModel for non-pipeline AI tasks. One row per
// (tenant, taskKey); the reserved SYSTEM tenant `00000000-…` row is the
// platform default. Resolution (AiTaskDefaultService.getEffective in
// packages/applications): tenant row → SYSTEM row → consuming service's env
// fallback. `modelSlug` references AiModel.slug within [tenant, SYSTEM] scope —
// no FK, per the AiModel slug-reference convention (see stt.prisma).
//
// Governance: the `guardrail.`, `nlp.`, and `harness.` task-key prefixes are
// SUPER_ADMIN-ONLY (service-level isSuperAdmin guard on writes) per
// SUPER_ADMIN_ONLY_TASK_PREFIXES in
// packages/applications/src/services/ai-task-default/constants.ts. For those,
// tenants only CONSUME the SYSTEM-row platform default and runtime resolution
// ignores per-tenant override rows. EXCEPTION: the `text.` prefix
// `text.live` / `text.finalize` and their `.fallback` variants — is tenant-admin
// configurable: tenants may write their own rows and runtime resolution honours
// them (tenant row → SYSTEM row).
// ============================================================================

model AiTaskDefault {
  // meta fields
  metaData Json?  @map("_metadata") @db.JsonB
  version  Int    @default(1) @map("_version")
  id       String @id @default(uuid(7))

  // multi tenant fields (SYSTEM tenant row = platform default)
  tenantId String

  // core fields
  taskKey    String // guardrail.validate | nlp.ner | nlp.classification
  modelSlug  String // references AiModel.slug (no FK — house convention)
  configJson Json?  @db.JsonB

  // the canonical task taxonomy this row's `taskKey` belongs to.
  // DERIVED from `taskKey`, never independently chosen: the mapping is
  // `AI_TASK_KIND_BY_TASK_KEY` in
  // `packages/applications/src/services/ai-task-default/constants.ts`.
  //
  // NULLABLE, on purpose. Phase 1 is purely ADDITIVE — it backfills every
  // existing row and changes no writer, so a row created by an un-migrated
  // writer lands NULL rather than carrying a plausible-but-wrong default.
  // "Nobody set it" is a state a resolver can fail closed on; a default of
  // TEXT_GENERATION would silently mislabel every `guardrail.*` and `nlp.*`
  // row, which is 8 of the 12 rows the seed creates. tightens this to
  // NOT NULL once `AiTaskDefaultService.upsertRow` sets it.
  taskKind AiTaskKind? // task-specific extras (thresholds, etc.)

  // resource status fields
  resourceStatus          ResourceStatusType @default(ENABLED)
  resourceStatusUpdatedAt DateTime?
  resourceStatusUpdatedBy String?

  // audit fields
  createdBy String?  @default("60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000")
  updatedBy String?
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  // indexing — one default per (tenant, task)
  @@unique([tenantId, taskKey], name: "AiTaskDefault_tenant_task_unique")
  @@index([tenantId], name: "AiTaskDefault_tenantId_idx")
  @@index([taskKey], name: "AiTaskDefault_taskKey_idx")
  // "every binding this tenant has for task kind X", the read
  // unified selection surface is built on. Leads with `tenantId` so
  // it also serves the plain tenant-scope reads the extension injects.
  @@index([tenantId, taskKind], name: "AiTaskDefault_tenantId_taskKind_idx")
  @@schema("core")
}
